The division of the imported clips into three sets (docs/plans/bodies-and-movement.md, phase 2
step 5): training.txt, test.txt and calibration.txt, a clip a line, as SOURCE/CLIP (the name of
the clip's files under .movement/poses/BODY/SOURCE/). A style of 100STYLE is wholly in one
set, chosen by the SHA-256 of its name modulo 10: 0 the test set, 1 the calibration set, the
rest training. So a net is tested on styles it never saw, and the judge is calibrated on others.
MPI EMBM's clips (two actors telling stories) are each in a set by the same rule on the clip's
own name.
CeTI-Age-Kinematics' clips (32 people, 30 daily tasks) are each in the set of their participant, by
the same rule on the participant's id (`sub-d02`): 26 people's 1,269 clips in training, 5 people's
245 in calibration, 1 person's 49 in test.
ACCAD's clips (its Open Motion Project's three performers, 296 of them) are each in a set by the
same rule on the clip's own name (`Male2_E1_JabLeft`): 241 in training, 28 in calibration, 27 in
test, Male 2's strikes, blocks and kicks among each.
